-absence. A known matching product with zero-stock options returns `out_of_stock`
+Unrecognized filters and ambiguous names ask for clarification. For a clearly named
+product, an exact customer-supplied name and a failed search against the complete
+permitted source catalog allow a checked natural `no_matches` reply, such as
+"দুঃখিত, আমাদের দোকানে বর্তমানে Claude নেই।" This is different from stock exhaustion.
+A known matching product with zero-stock options returns `out_of_stock`
 and its current details; the browser displays those details without a checkout
 link. Saved descriptions and size charts remain accessible in the product card.
 Offline regressions include synthetic drop-shoulder / No Love / size / product-switch
 conversations, invalid/foreign IDs and stale stock. Live merchant catalog publication
 and real-provider interpretation remain unverified by those fixtures.
+
+Focused regressions additionally cover two published shops, scalar/list product FAQ
+scope, current prices/settings/knowledge after reindexing, long-document retrieval,
+Bangla/Banglish/English and saved language overrides, digital terms/warranty,
+credential exclusion, unavailable sources, fabricated commerce claims and malicious
+knowledge/prompt-extraction attempts. A shared policy-validator fix recognizes the
+ordinary English wording "There is no warranty" without accepting conditional or
+invented warranties. These finite checks reduce unsupported claims; they are not a
+guarantee of exhaustive semantic verification or identical model wording across channels.
